   ? @v1 == 2 [
    "Zero Web capabilities - experimental local document preview\n\nInput: local HTML or ZTEXT001; at most 65536 document bytes and 512 nodes.\nNetwork protocols: none in this native preview. No HTTP, HTTPS or TLS fetching.\nHTML: bounded element/text tree, id/class/style, entities, style and script data.\nCSS: single tag, .class, #id and * selectors; source order, specificity and inline priority.\nCSS properties: color, background-color, font-size, display, padding, margin, width.\nLayout: bounded block/inline flow, BR line breaks, word wrapping and scrolling.\nDrawing: own 800 x 600 RGB raster and bitmap font; non-ASCII glyphs use placeholders.\nJavaScript: bounded let/const/var, assignment, integer/string + expressions and\n  document.getElementById(...).textContent; not full ECMAScript or a browser DOM.\nScripts have no network, filesystem, process, eval or import interface.\nExternal script sources are rejected. No Python interpreter is included.\nPython on a remote server is separate from the documents a browser receives.\nGUI: local X11/Xwayland on Linux; Win32 on Windows; keyboard/wheel scrolling.\nOutput: visible-text inspection, supported-profile check, exclusive-create Zpix raster.\n\nNot implemented: URL navigation, TLS, full HTML5/CSS/ECMAScript, CSS flex/grid,\nweb media playback, web fonts, full Unicode glyphs or Chromium compatibility.\nUnsupported page features can be rejected or reported with a profile warning.\nThis list describes the native preview, not the separate Zero OS HTTP text reader.\n\nBuilt-in information page: zero-web --about\nOwn diagnostic page: zero-web browser/engine/capabilities-demo.ztext\nIt exercises CSS priority, display:none, BR and JavaScript textContent.\nHeadless diagnostics: --check INPUT, --inspect INPUT, --render INPUT NEW.zpix\nEngine regression checks: zero-web-check\n" -> @v5.
